# Byte preservation for relocated qualification evidence.
#
# Every entry in artifact-manifest.sha256 is a SHA-256 over exact bytes. The
# umbrella .gitattributes sets only `* whitespace=cr-at-eol`; it pins no text or
# eol handling, so on a clone with core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) Git
# would rewrite these files' line endings on checkout and every text entry would
# stop matching its manifest hash. `-text` disables that conversion in both
# directions.
#
# `-whitespace` additionally stops `git diff --check` and whitespace-fixing
# hooks reporting the trailing whitespace and blank-at-EOF that five relocated
# evidence files genuinely contain (logs/builds-3102/evidence-direct-full.log,
# logs/builds-3102/diag-module/*.diag, logs/builds-3701/03e-module-tests-diag.log,
# logs/eventstore-3102/remote-01-restore.log, p1r-diff.txt). Those bytes are the
# evidence; they must never be "fixed".
#
# The four files authored for this bundle (README.md, .gitignore, .gitattributes,
# manifest-verification.txt) deliberately keep whitespace checking.
* -text
logs/** -whitespace
results/** -whitespace
retained-packages/** -whitespace
remote-consumer-3102/** -whitespace
p1r-diff.txt -whitespace
release-packages-3.102.0.json -whitespace
release-packages-3.70.1.json -whitespace
*.nupkg binary
*.snupkg binary
